WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.298
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.298 --> 00:00:05.006
My name is Lily Ma and my
one word is extraordinary.

00:00:05.006 --> 00:00:07.022
I believe that every single human being

00:00:07.022 --> 00:00:09.381
is capable of extraordinary things.

00:00:09.381 --> 00:00:11.299
So, to help you on your journey,

00:00:11.299 --> 00:00:13.739
today's message is create your own luck.

00:00:13.739 --> 00:00:16.062
Over to you, Donald Trump.

00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:17.754
(rooster crows)

00:00:17.754 --> 00:00:20.477
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:20.477 --> 00:00:23.280
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.199
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:28.708
What would be one word of advice

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:31.188
you would have for an
upcoming businessman,

00:00:31.188 --> 00:00:33.271
for a future businessman?

00:00:34.512 --> 00:00:35.345
- Uhm.

00:00:35.345 --> 00:00:36.330
- Or a woman.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.861
- Knowledge. Knowledge.

00:00:38.861 --> 00:00:39.852
But if it's one word.

00:00:39.852 --> 00:00:42.923
One word's very hard for that,
but the word is knowledge.

00:00:42.923 --> 00:00:45.921
But you get knowledge through experience.

00:00:45.921 --> 00:00:48.184
One of the things people
talk about is luck,

00:00:48.184 --> 00:00:50.146
and I do believe that people are lucky

00:00:50.146 --> 00:00:51.676
and some people are luckier than others.

00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:53.199
I do believe that.

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:54.330
But there's also an expression,

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.872
the harder you work, the luckier you get.

00:00:56.872 --> 00:01:00.703
And I can tell you 10
instances where I didn't quit.

00:01:00.703 --> 00:01:03.770
One, it was 1990, the
world was coming down,

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.033
the debt markets were down,

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:07.271
everybody all of my friends and enemies

00:01:07.271 --> 00:01:10.021
were going bankrupt, I never did.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:13.906
The times were, actually just terrible.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.449
And even today, you look at times

00:01:15.449 --> 00:01:17.665
and you see what happens
and you have to learn.

00:01:17.665 --> 00:01:20.089
But, the word luck is very interesting,

00:01:20.089 --> 00:01:22.849
but if I didn't work really hard,

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:26.238
I'd probably would not,
almost definitely would not

00:01:26.238 --> 00:01:28.524
be here today and unless you had me up

00:01:28.524 --> 00:01:32.443
as a man who at one point was successful,

00:01:32.443 --> 00:01:35.147
but let's see what a loser looks like.

00:01:35.147 --> 00:01:38.805
So you have to work
hard because it is true.

00:01:38.805 --> 00:01:41.804
You can develop luck through hard work.

00:01:41.804 --> 00:01:45.791
- So I think luck plays a
part in people's success,

00:01:45.791 --> 00:01:48.355
but a really small part.

00:01:48.355 --> 00:01:51.991
It becomes a problem if
that's all you focus on.

00:01:51.991 --> 00:01:55.930
It becomes a problem when
you use it as an excuse

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:58.517
not to go out there and do
something with your life.

00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:02.370
It becomes an even bigger
problem if you're always waiting

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.691
for luck to come your way.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:07.952
So for example, I'm just
starting out as a speaker.

00:02:07.952 --> 00:02:10.742
I'm in my early stages
of my speaking career.

00:02:10.742 --> 00:02:12.412
I look at Evan.

00:02:12.412 --> 00:02:14.678
He just went to Paris
and he spoke in front of

00:02:14.678 --> 00:02:16.242
thousands of people,

00:02:16.242 --> 00:02:18.311
ate at a fancy restaurant,

00:02:18.311 --> 00:02:20.939
sat at first-class airlines,

00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:23.003
went to a beautiful hotel,

00:02:23.003 --> 00:02:25.171
and he was given this opportunity

00:02:25.171 --> 00:02:26.754
and he is so lucky.

00:02:27.836 --> 00:02:28.986
Right?

00:02:28.986 --> 00:02:31.980
That is not the mindset
that I need to have.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.614
That kind of mindset will
completely destroy my future

00:02:35.614 --> 00:02:37.781
and will not help me grow.

00:02:38.836 --> 00:02:42.507
The reason why Evan had that opportunity

00:02:42.507 --> 00:02:47.299
is through years and years of
dedicated hard work over time.

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:48.875
I work with that man.

00:02:48.875 --> 00:02:50.898
I know how consistent he is.

00:02:50.898 --> 00:02:52.524
I know how determined he is.

00:02:52.524 --> 00:02:56.988
And I know how dedicated
he is to his mission.

00:02:56.988 --> 00:02:58.788
And the reason why I don't have

00:02:58.788 --> 00:03:01.309
that luck or that opportunity,

00:03:01.309 --> 00:03:04.274
is because I don't deserve it yet.

00:03:04.274 --> 00:03:08.308
And it's no way for me to
knock myself down at all.

00:03:08.308 --> 00:03:11.134
Instead, it raises me even higher

00:03:11.134 --> 00:03:14.826
because I am not waiting
for some elusive fairy

00:03:14.826 --> 00:03:18.072
to come around and
sprinkle dust over my head

00:03:18.072 --> 00:03:20.869
that is called luck for this to happen.

00:03:20.869 --> 00:03:22.673
It is within my control.

00:03:22.673 --> 00:03:24.783
I have the responsibility
and accountability

00:03:24.783 --> 00:03:26.733
to make that happen for myself.

00:03:26.733 --> 00:03:27.884
I need to work harder.

00:03:27.884 --> 00:03:30.063
I need to work harder
consistently over time,

00:03:30.063 --> 00:03:31.319
keep working, keep working,

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:32.639
be dedicated to my mission,

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:34.856
keep working, gain
knowledge through research,

00:03:34.856 --> 00:03:39.844
and soon enough that
opportunity will come my way.

00:03:39.844 --> 00:03:41.940
So next time you look at someone

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.496
that you think has a lot
of luck in their life,

00:03:46.496 --> 00:03:50.539
change your mindset around and find ways

00:03:50.539 --> 00:03:52.485
to create your own luck.

00:03:52.485 --> 00:03:53.790
So the question of the day is,

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.038
what is that one
opportunity you really want

00:03:57.038 --> 00:04:00.218
in your life that hasn't
happened for you yet?

00:04:00.218 --> 00:04:01.991
And hopefully when you write it down,

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:03.888
it's going to give you the fuel, the fire

00:04:03.888 --> 00:04:05.780
to go and make your own luck.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:06.897
So leave in the comments below

00:04:06.897 --> 00:04:08.879
and I'll join in on the discussion.

00:04:08.879 --> 00:04:11.255
So I also have a quick
shout out for Evan Lieanto,

00:04:11.255 --> 00:04:13.027
thank you so much for picking up a copy of

00:04:13.027 --> 00:04:15.268
Evan's book, Your One Word.

00:04:15.268 --> 00:04:16.924
Your support means a lot to us

00:04:16.924 --> 00:04:18.886
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:04:18.886 --> 00:04:20.235
So thank you so much for watching.

00:04:20.235 --> 00:04:21.773
I believe in you and I hope you

00:04:21.773 --> 00:04:24.331
continue to believe in yourself

00:04:24.331 --> 00:04:26.219
and whatever your one word is

00:04:26.219 --> 00:04:28.021
and we'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:04:28.021 --> 00:04:30.351
for another shot of espresso.

00:04:30.351 --> 00:04:33.035
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:33.035 --> 00:04:36.452
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:04:39.918 --> 00:04:41.909
- I think that's one
of the strongest things

00:04:41.909 --> 00:04:44.409
you can cultivate as an entrepreneur

00:04:44.409 --> 00:04:46.326
is to not rely on luck,

00:04:47.218 --> 00:04:50.349
but cultivating an ability to recognize

00:04:50.349 --> 00:04:53.446
fortunate situations
when they're occurring.

00:04:53.446 --> 00:04:55.692
Odeo was a very fortunate situation.

00:04:55.692 --> 00:04:56.843
Could've taken that idea,

00:04:56.843 --> 00:05:01.202
not told it to Ev, not told
it to Biz, not told it to Noah

00:05:01.202 --> 00:05:03.600
and all my other coworkers at Odeo

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.598
and tried to start my own
company with that idea.

00:05:06.598 --> 00:05:08.194
But the fortunate situation was that

00:05:08.194 --> 00:05:10.188
I was working with some
really amazing people

00:05:10.188 --> 00:05:12.188
and we had a great team.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:16.820
And so of course it makes
sense to start there.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.062
The fortunate situation for Square,

00:05:19.062 --> 00:05:21.895
was that in 2008, the end of 2008,

00:05:22.958 --> 00:05:25.183
the entire market was crashing down.

00:05:25.183 --> 00:05:27.773
All of these abstractions we built upon,

00:05:27.773 --> 00:05:30.802
abstraction upon
abstraction upon abstraction

00:05:30.802 --> 00:05:34.493
in the financial world which
no single human understood,

00:05:34.493 --> 00:05:36.493
were now falling apart and suddenly

00:05:36.493 --> 00:05:39.724
we're getting back to
basics, back to fundamentals,

00:05:39.724 --> 00:05:41.609
management teams were
being asked to leave,

00:05:41.609 --> 00:05:45.854
banks were failing, people
were clarifying around

00:05:45.854 --> 00:05:48.068
we need to start getting innovative,

00:05:48.068 --> 00:05:51.326
we need to stop treating
our customers so poorly,

00:05:51.326 --> 00:05:55.493
we need to stop encouraging
bad behavior that reap fees.

00:05:56.341 --> 00:05:58.784
Like, we really need to turn
this whole thing around.

00:05:58.784 --> 00:06:01.434
And anytime there's a
recession or a depression,

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:04.280
that's a great time to
innovate, start a company,

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.697
start a project, do anything.

00:06:09.663 --> 00:06:11.842
We recognize that time

00:06:11.842 --> 00:06:15.175
and at the same time, my co-founder Jim,

00:06:17.437 --> 00:06:20.051
he contacted me, I've known
him since I was 15 years old,

00:06:20.051 --> 00:06:23.022
he was my boss when I was 15 years old.

00:06:23.022 --> 00:06:25.310
And, he's like, Jack
I want to talk to you.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:28.430
I want to build an electronic car company.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:31.223
That's interesting and
he was thinking about it

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:34.271
because the car industry
was failing as well.

00:06:34.271 --> 00:06:36.442
He's like, why don't we just
give these car companies

00:06:36.442 --> 00:06:38.684
to well-seasoned entrepreneurs.

00:06:38.684 --> 00:06:41.811
Why don't we Ford to Steve Jobs.

00:06:41.811 --> 00:06:42.850
- That would be amazing.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:45.183
- Yeah, it would be amazing.

00:06:46.085 --> 00:06:48.718
And GM to Ellison or whatnot

00:06:48.718 --> 00:06:51.084
and also I want to start
an electronic car company

00:06:51.084 --> 00:06:53.835
and I'm like, that's ambitious.

00:06:53.835 --> 00:06:55.089
But in that moment we decided

00:06:55.089 --> 00:06:56.773
not to start an electronic car company,

00:06:56.773 --> 00:06:59.325
but we wanted to do something together.

00:06:59.325 --> 00:07:01.217
And we kept having these
weekly conversations

00:07:01.217 --> 00:07:02.934
about what that thing was.

00:07:02.934 --> 00:07:05.691
And I was researching a lot
with finance and healthcare

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:09.392
because I was looking at doing
something in those spaces.

00:07:09.392 --> 00:07:12.098
And Jim called me one day in one of those

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:15.289
scheduled meetings and he said,

00:07:15.289 --> 00:07:18.087
I just lost a glass sale.

00:07:18.087 --> 00:07:20.911
He's an artist; he sells glass.

00:07:20.911 --> 00:07:23.952
And I lost the sale because I
couldn't accept a credit card.

00:07:23.952 --> 00:07:26.014
And here he was talking on his iPhone,

00:07:26.014 --> 00:07:27.570
this general purpose computer

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:29.463
and I was talking on my iPhone.

00:07:29.463 --> 00:07:32.090
- A one gigahertz computer
sitting in the palm of your hand

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.309
but no way to accept credit cards.

00:07:33.309 --> 00:07:35.693
- He couldn't accept $2,000 from someone

00:07:35.693 --> 00:07:38.403
who wanted to pay him, why is that?

00:07:38.403 --> 00:07:41.308
So we decided that we wanted
to answer that question.

00:07:41.308 --> 00:07:42.522
And we did a bunch of research,

00:07:42.522 --> 00:07:44.868
I started writing some server code

00:07:44.868 --> 00:07:48.101
and we hired a guy to
write some iPhone code

00:07:48.101 --> 00:07:49.448
and Jim built some hardware

00:07:49.448 --> 00:07:51.870
and in a month we had a little,

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:54.629
well, it was actually quite a big device

00:07:54.629 --> 00:07:57.285
that plugged into the
audio jack of your iPhone

00:07:57.285 --> 00:08:00.249
and could swipe a card, take a payment,

00:08:00.249 --> 00:08:01.993
it would go through the merchant process

00:08:01.993 --> 00:08:05.028
and then generate a
receipt with a map on it.

00:08:05.028 --> 00:08:08.820
I went around and showed
it to a bunch of investors.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:12.570
They were all amazed
that it could even work.

00:08:13.748 --> 00:08:18.257
So we decided to really focus
on it and make it a company.

00:08:18.257 --> 00:08:20.463
It really just comes down to recognizing

00:08:20.463 --> 00:08:22.241
that fortunate situation and recognizing

00:08:22.241 --> 00:08:23.921
the people around you that could help

00:08:23.921 --> 00:08:25.754
and just honing it.

00:08:25.754 --> 00:08:27.444
- You were bold, you
kind of talked him up,

00:08:27.444 --> 00:08:31.114
you ended up selling his
house but you approached him

00:08:31.114 --> 00:08:33.158
and you said, are you ready
to sell one of your houses?

00:08:33.158 --> 00:08:34.919
You already knew that he owned two houses,

00:08:34.919 --> 00:08:36.184
you knew where they were,

00:08:36.184 --> 00:08:38.587
so isn't that also a big part of this.

00:08:38.587 --> 00:08:40.577
You have to really do the hard work?

00:08:40.577 --> 00:08:43.672
- Yeah and really preparing
yourself to be lucky.

00:08:43.672 --> 00:08:47.205
Putting yourself in situations
where you can get lucky.

00:08:47.205 --> 00:08:49.665
Where it's not so much
luck, it's preparation.

00:08:49.665 --> 00:08:51.176
I tell a story about how I'm standing

00:08:51.176 --> 00:08:53.566
inside a line at Starbucks,

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:55.594
and I'm not at that Starbucks
because I like coffee,

00:08:55.594 --> 00:08:56.942
I'm at that Starbucks because that's

00:08:56.942 --> 00:08:59.168
where all the wealthy people
and all the celebrities

00:08:59.168 --> 00:09:01.406
in Beverly Hills go every morning.

00:09:01.406 --> 00:09:02.659
I meet a guy in line in front of me,

00:09:02.659 --> 00:09:05.025
I end up showing him a
house later that afternoon

00:09:05.025 --> 00:09:06.768
and he buys a 12 million dollar house.

00:09:06.768 --> 00:09:08.285
Some people will say that's luck.

00:09:08.285 --> 00:09:10.686
For me, it's all about
being at the right place

00:09:10.686 --> 00:09:12.402
and there was a reason why I'm there

00:09:12.402 --> 00:09:13.907
because I'm an expert in my community

00:09:13.907 --> 00:09:16.137
and I put myself in that situation.

